<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dakar (Adal)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dakar, or Dakkar, was a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> that served as a capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>. The sultanate's administrative capital shifted from the coastal port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> to Dakar and eventually to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harar">Harar</a>. The moves reflected the Adal Sultanate's gradual reorientation toward the interior.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Sabr ad-Din III reconstituted the Walashma state in the eastern lowlands of Adal, with its seat at <b>Dakkar</b> near Harar and the port of Zeila as its commercial outlet, a strategic choice that placed the new sultanate further from Ethiopian power while preserving access to the lucrative Red…</blockquote><a href="/empire/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
